erience it  visually it's exciting from scaling  smokestacks in Prague to climbing  skyscrapers in Tokyo the performers body  always becomes a graphic element in the  image a symbol in the cityscape the  compositions are carefully thought  through the danger seems to be of  secondary importance it's been done  divorced in the moment when I do this  I'm very conscious of the moment and as  I get older I enjoy these moments more  and more when I managed to make a dream  reality and to do the things that up to  then I'd only envision for a new-build  I'm coaxing  the films have a poetic serene quality  with the danger barely perceptible this  conflict is what makes the art of Matias  Bianca and Michelin cough so powerful  and what has already earned them several  awards the question now is how far this  risky road will take them  because in Tata we've reached a point  where things are starting to change  we're trying to reduce the images to the  essential and we've realized that the  risk aspect is getting in the way that  many viewers just can't see past the  danger and appreciate the imagery for  what it is so we're looking for some way  to reduce that aspect yeah of not  invasive this also games  whichever way their art goes from here  the duo's daring exploits are not over  yet
 

